# Secret Message Encoder - Logbook 01: Project Outline

this file will work as the beginning of my project, and where i will decide on and outline the main functions of my secret message encoder.

## success criteria:
- will work with both strings and integers
- presents the option for the user to choose a type of cipher (ceaser, vicinere, XOR)
- will allow a decrypt option
- will generate a key for encrypted message
- code will test for errors, like floating points, no message entered etc

since, provided in the spec, the program is supposed to work from the command line, the code will function within a cmd window. the structure will be:

```text
cipher_project/
├── main.py          <-- Runs in cmd, grabs arguments, generates random key
├── caesar.py        <-- Contains caesar_encode()
├── vigenere.py      <-- Contains vigenere_encode()
└── xor_cipher.py    <-- Contains xor_encode()
```


